From: DotRedstone <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: program SM8550 UFS UniPro rates

U-Boot exposes the SM8550 UFS UniPro clock gate but has no set_rate path.
Add the 75, 150 and 300 MHz table and program its 0x77098 RCG.

Source: DotRedstone/linux-sheng commit c4b27e2cec1371e166f443877812639d4d0d33da,
drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c (GPL-2.0-only). The register offset and
frequency/parent/divider tuples are transcribed from the pinned Linux source;
this patch adapts them to U-Boot's existing clk_rcg_set_rate_mnd API.

This only makes the UFS driver's requested UniPro rates programmable. It does
not establish UFS power, PHY calibration, storage discovery, or boot safety.

Signed-off-by: DotRedstone <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c
index 7c06489..cfe8472 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c
@@ -69,0 +70,7 @@ static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_gcc_pcie_0_phy_rchng_clk_src[] = {
+static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_gcc_ufs_phy_unipro_core_clk_src[] = {
+	F(75000000, CFG_CLK_SRC_GPLL0_EVEN, 4, 0, 0),
+	F(150000000, CFG_CLK_SRC_GPLL0, 4, 0, 0),
+	F(300000000, CFG_CLK_SRC_GPLL0, 2, 0, 0),
+	{ }
+};
+
@@ -90,0 +98,5 @@ static ulong sm8550_set_rate(struct clk *clk, ulong rate)
+	case GCC_UFS_PHY_UNIPRO_CORE_CLK:
+		freq = qcom_find_freq(ftbl_gcc_ufs_phy_unipro_core_clk_src, rate);
+		clk_rcg_set_rate_mnd(priv->base, 0x77098,
+				     freq->pre_div, freq->m, freq->n, freq->src, 8);
+		return freq->freq;
